{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2155-12-16 03:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be taking care of you during this hospital stay. Can you tell me what brought you in tonight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2155-12-16 03:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve had this sharp stomach pain since yesterday, along with nausea, vomiting, and watery diarrhea. It’s just like the last time I was here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2155-12-16 03:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned it’s similar to your last episode. Was that treated with rifaximin and hyoscyamine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2155-12-16 03:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. That helped before, but it came back. The pain is worse this time, and I’m waking up at night from the diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2155-12-16 03:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks for that. We’ve started you on IV fluids and some pain medication. We’ll run some tests to make sure nothing else is going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2155-12-16 03:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I also had a little cough and chills. Is that part of this?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2155-12-16 03:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll check for infections, but it could be a mild viral thing. Your vitals are stable, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from last night are mostly normal. Your liver enzymes were a bit high, but not concerning. No signs of kidney issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about the diarrhea? I’m still having some."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We tested your stool. No C. diff, no salmonella, shigella, or other bacteria. So it’s not an active infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing it then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history, we think it’s a flare of small intestinal bacterial overgrowth—SIBO. That’s what we treated last time, and it responded well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So we’re doing the same treatment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2155-12-16 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re restarting rifaximin and hyoscyamine. They stay in the gut and help reduce the bacteria and your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2155-12-16 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling now? Any improvement?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2155-12-16 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The pain is a little better. I haven’t vomited since this morning. But I’m still bloated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2155-12-16 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. We’ll keep you on IV fluids for now and advance your diet slowly. We also checked your CMV—came back negative, so that’s not contributing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2155-12-16 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about that. What about my immune system? I know my IgG was low last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2155-12-16 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your IgG was 698 this morning—just below normal. We’re going to give you IVIG to boost it. It may help with both your gut symptoms and GVHD."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2155-12-16 14:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that make me feel better overall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2155-12-16 14:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should help your immunity and may reduce inflammation from GVHD. We’ll check your levels again as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2155-12-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You’re doing well. Your pain is improving, and you kept down breakfast. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2155-12-17 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I feel like I can eat more now. Is the IVIG helping already?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2155-12-17 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It takes time, but we’re on the right track. Your GI team agrees—this is likely SIBO and gut GVHD. No need for more scans."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2155-12-17 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember last time they found a cyst on my pancreas. Should we check that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2155-12-17 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but it’s stable and not causing symptoms. You’ll follow up with GI for a breath test to confirm SIBO and monitor the cyst."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2155-12-18 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat stool tests are negative again. No parasites, no viruses isolated so far. Norovirus is still pending."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2155-12-18 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So still no infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2155-12-18 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. That supports our diagnosis of SIBO, not an acute infection. Your pain is much better, and you’ve had no diarrhea since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2155-12-18 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2155-12-18 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re getting there. We’ll watch you for one more day to make sure you stay stable on oral meds and food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2155-12-18 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, we arranged for autologous eye drops for your dry eyes from GVHD. You’ll get those soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2155-12-18 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My vision’s been blurry. I’m glad we’re addressing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2155-12-19 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You made it through the night without symptoms. Great job. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow if all goes well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2155-12-19 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. What meds will I be on at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2155-12-19 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching from rifaximin to Augmentin for one more week. It covers a broader range of gut bacteria."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2155-12-19 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And the hyoscyamine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2155-12-19 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue that three times a day. Also keep taking your omeprazole, prednisone, and other regular meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2155-12-19 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my pain medicine? I’m on MS Contin now twice a day instead of three times."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2155-12-19 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right. We lowered it because your pain is better. If it flares up, we can increase it. Use the immediate-release oxycodone for breakthrough pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2155-12-19 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning are stable. Hemoglobin is a bit low, but not new. We’ll check iron for your restless legs later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2155-12-19 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That tingling in my legs at night has been worse. I hope iron helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2155-12-19 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might. We’ll discuss that with your hematologist at your follow-up in three weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2155-12-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge tomorrow. You’ve had no pain, no diarrhea, and you’re eating well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2155-12-20 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Any diet changes I should follow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2155-12-20 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Limit dairy—lactose can worsen bloating. If you eat dairy, take Lactaid. For beans, use Beano to reduce gas."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2155-12-20 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my appointments?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2155-12-20 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "GI follow-up is scheduled. You’ll get the SIBO breath test there. And hematology for IgG check and possible IVIG if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2155-12-20 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make sure to go. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2155-12-20 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll see you in clinic. Call if you have fever, severe pain, or diarrhea returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before you leave. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really good. No pain, no issues. Ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Remember: take Augmentin with food, keep using hyoscyamine, and follow the diet tips."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Take care, and we’ll see you at your follow-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2155-12-21 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2155-12-16 03:04:00",
    "admission_end": "2155-12-21 18:51:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with an acute exacerbation of chronic abdominal pain and diarrhea, consistent with her prior episodes. She was treated with rifaximin and hyoscyamine, with significant improvement in symptoms. Workup showed no infectious cause, supporting a diagnosis of small intestinal bacterial overgrowth. Hypogammaglobulinemia was confirmed with a low IgG level, and she received IVIG to support immune function. Her nausea and vomiting resolved, and she tolerated oral intake well. She was transitioned to Augmentin for continued treatment of bacterial overgrowth and discharged home with follow-up appointments in GI and hematology. Her chronic graft-versus-host disease was managed with ongoing prednisone and new autologous eye drops for ocular symptoms.",
    "problems": [
      "Other specified disorders of intestine",
      "Complications of transplanted bone marrow",
      "Chronic myeloid leukemia, without mention of having achieved remission",
      "Chronic graft-versus-host disease",
      "Hypogammaglobulinemia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
